{
  "mn70:0.1": "Middle Discourses 70 ",
  "mn70:0.2": "At Kīṭāgiri ",
  "mn70:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn70:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was wandering in the land of the Kāsis together with a large Saṅgha of mendicants. ",
  "mn70:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants: ",
  "mn70:2.1": "“Mendicants, I abstain from eating at night. ",
  "mn70:2.2": "Doing so, I find that I’m healthy and well, nimble, strong, and living comfortably. ",
  "mn70:2.3": "You too should never eat at night. ",
  "mn70:2.4": "Doing so, you’ll find that you’re healthy and well, nimble, strong, and living comfortably.” ",
  "mn70:2.5": "“Yes, sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn70:3.1": "Then the Buddha, traveling stage by stage in the land of the Kāsis, arrived at a town of the Kāsis named Kīṭāgiri, ",
  "mn70:3.2": "and stayed there. ",
  "mn70:4.1": "Now at that time the mendicants who followed Assaji and Punabbasuka were residing at Kīṭāgiri. ",
  "mn70:4.2": "Then several mendicants went up to them and said, ",
  "mn70:4.3": "“Reverends, the Buddha never eats at night, and neither does the mendicant Saṅgha. ",
  "mn70:4.4": "Doing so, they find that they’re healthy and well, nimble, strong, and living comfortably. ",
  "mn70:4.5": "You too should abstain from eating at night. ",
  "mn70:4.6": "Doing so, you’ll find that you’re healthy and well, nimble, strong, and living comfortably.” ",
  "mn70:4.7": "When they said this, the mendicants who followed Assaji and Punabbasuka said to 